# Copy this file to .env, in this same folder, and put your real key in it:
#
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# .env is in .gitignore and must never be committed. This file is the
# template and holds no real key; brain.py refuses to run with the
# placeholder below.
#
# Creating .env on Windows:
#   copy .env.example .env            (cmd)  -- then edit the key in Notepad
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env       (PowerShell)
# Do NOT use PowerShell's  echo ... > .env  : Windows PowerShell writes that
# as UTF-16. (brain.py now reads it anyway, but other tools will not.)
# If you save from Notepad, choose "Save as type: All files", or you get
# .env.txt, which nothing reads.
#
# Only make.py --auto and auto.py need a key, and only the one for the
# provider chosen in config.yaml (llm.provider): ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for
# claude_api, GEMINI_API_KEY for gemini, none for claude_code, which uses
# your Claude Code sign-in. Rendering a storyboard you wrote yourself
# never touches a model.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-REPLACE-ME

# For llm.provider: gemini -- a free key from Google AI Studio.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
